<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ming Rui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1768</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ming Rui was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>, a relative by marriage of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qianlong-emperor">Qianlong Emperor</a>, who commanded the third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-burmese-war-1765-1769">Qing invasion of Burma</a> in 1767–1768. After advancing towards Ava, his army was cut off and destroyed by Burmese forces near Maymyo in early 1768, and he took his own life rather than be captured. He had earlier served in the Qing campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ming-rui.jpg" alt="Ming Rui" width="320" height="602" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mingrui.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
